default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-16T13:57:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T14:11:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.7 stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable (5b4e0cb0f) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Tue, 07 Jul 2026 05:05:48 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 Ti (nvidia; 580.173.02) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 19.44 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nSome might not be aware that to append an array, even if the array to append is a single element, you have to use the append_array() function. \n\nIt would be nice to have the editor throw an error or warning instead of failing silently.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```gdscript\nvar Arr: Array[Dictionary]\nvar Appending: Array[Dictionary]\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n    Arr.append(Appending) # This will fail silently.\n    Arr.append_array(Appending) # This is the correct way.\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121454/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121454/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}